(2. NOMINAL COMPOUNDS & GENDER MARKERS) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Compounding is the most productive lexical expansion mechanism in) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Tangkhul. Compounds exhibit head-initial and head-final constructions.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Natural gender in animate nouns is marked not by grammatical inflection) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(but by sex-specifying enclitics: -va for feminine \(e.g. siva 'bitch',) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(harva 'hen'\) and -mayar for masculine \(simayar 'male dog', harmayar) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
('rooster'\).) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
(Tangkhul Linguistic Data & Analysis:) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(  * mayarnao \(man/son\) / ngalanao \(woman/daughter\) : Human gender terms) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(    Analysis: Root + gender enclitic + diminutive nao.) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 9 Tf
